# G8 Flow — QA (apply what fits; skip what doesn’t)

Sources filtered for a freelancer service portfolio (not ecommerce, not local-service map packs, not SaaS onboarding unless added later). Full notes: `docs/g8-flow/qa-checklists.md`.

## Always apply

- Hero: clear value H1, supporting line, dominant visual, **2 CTAs**, trust near CTAs
- Benefits = outcomes; process = 3–5 linear steps
- Proof: case results + named testimonials with photos
- Pricing: max 3 plans, highlight one, CTA on each
- One primary conversion goal sitewide (e.g. book call) + soft secondary
- Mobile: 44px targets, readable type, no hover-only actions
- Perf: LCP/CLS/INP budgets; WebP/AVIF; lazy non-critical; font-display swap; particle FX must not tank mobile
- SEO: unique title/meta, one H1, logical H2s, OG image, alt text, sitemap/robots at launch
- A11y: contrast on navy/blue, focus states, carousel keyboard support, reduced-motion fallback for hero particles
- Launch: HTTPS, 404, analytics events on CTAs, privacy/terms in footer, no lorem/placeholders

## Skip / de-emphasize

- Ecommerce cart/checkout, product schema, shipping
- Local SEO (GMB, NAP, service-area pages) unless user asks
- Fake countdown / scarcity badges
- Heavy competitor comparison tables
- Multi-language hreflang until i18n is in scope
- Blog content machinery on v1 homepage

## Conflict rule

If a checklist item conflicts with G8 brand, section architecture, or Hormozi copy rules — **G8 rules win**.
